--- !u!114 &-981249408119489314
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Let''s open the VFX asset used to control the Butterflies VFX.


      1. In the <i>Project</i> window, go to <b>SampleSceneAssets</b> > <b>Particles</b> and open <b>Butterflies.vfx.</b>


      2. Find the <b>Spawn</b> block at the top of the graph and disconnect the <b>Count</b> node.


      3. In the <b>Spawn</b> block, increase the <b>Count</b> to 50.


      4. Select <b>Compile</b> at the top left of the window to refresh the VFX.


      Notice that many more butterflies are flying in the tree cage.'
